[{:db/id 17592186171860 :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y) =  \\left\\langle ye^{xy},\\, xe^{xy}\\right\\rangle$ and the points $A(1,1)$ and $B(2,2)$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\mathbf F$ is conservative.\n\nII. $\\displaystyle\\int\\limits_{C_1} \\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r = e^4-e,$ where $C_1$ is the path along the curve $y=\\sqrt{2x},$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$\n\nIII. $\\displaystyle\\int\\limits_{C_2} \\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r = e^4-e,$ where $C_2$ is the path along along the line segment $\\overline{AB},$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172300 :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=⟨{e}^{x+y},\\,{e}^{x+y}⟩$ and the points $O(0,0)$ and $A(1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $F$ is conservative.\n\nII. ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=2e-1,$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the line segment $\\overset{―}{OA},$ traversed from $O$ to $A.$\n\nIII. ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=2e-1,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1),$ traversed from $O$ to $A.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186415272 :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=⟨{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\,{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y⟩$ and the points $O(0,0)$ and $A(1,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $F$ is conservative.\n\nII. ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=e,$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the line segment $\\overset{―}{OA},$ traversed from $O$ to $A.$\n\nIII. ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=2e-1,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the curve $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\sqrt{x},$ traversed from $O$ to $A.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186419017 :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=⟨-y,\\,x⟩$ and the points $A(0,1)$ and $B(0,-1)$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne 0,$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ traversed from $A$ to $B$ in counterclockwise direction.\n\nII. ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the segment line $\\overset{―}{AB},$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$\n\nIII. ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ is independent of path.\n\nIV. $F$ is conservative." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186415281 :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=⟨{e}^{y},\\,x{e}^{y}⟩$ and the points $A(1,0)$ and $B(3,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $F$ is conservative.\n\nII. ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=8,$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x),$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$\n\nIII. ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=3,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB},$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186415275 :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=⟨y,\\,x⟩$ and the points $O(0,0)$ and $A(\\sqrt{2},2)$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $F$ is conservative.\n\nII. ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=2\\sqrt{2},$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the line segment $\\overset{―}{OA},$ traversed from $O$ to $A.$\n\nIII. ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=-\\sqrt{2},$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the curve $y={x}^{2},$ traversed from $O$ to $A.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
